WEBVTT

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.880
- Hello, I'm Bob Ross, and I'd like to welcome you

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.510
to the 16th Joy of Paintings series.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:24.180
First of all, let me thank you for inviting me back

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:26.580
for another series of painting shows.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.330
If this is your first time with us,

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:30.000
let me extend a personal invitation

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:32.970
for you to get out your old brushes and your oil paints

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:34.810
and paint along with us each show.

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:36.570
Or just pull up the old easy chair,

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:39.150
put your foots up, and enjoy a relaxing half hour

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:42.500
as we play some of nature's masterpieces on canvas.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:43.990
Tell you what, let's start out

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:46.190
by having to run all the colors across the screen

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:48.250
that you need to paint along with me.

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:50.090
And while they're doing that, come on, let's go up here

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:52.110
and let me show you what I've already done.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:54.500
I've got two canvases up here today.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:56.360
We thought we'd do something a little different.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:58.080
I get a lot of requests from people

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.000
wanting to do like winter and summer

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.920
or the different scenes, so I thought today

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:05.650
I would show you how to do two paintings at one time.

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:08.280
And this will be your challenge for the day.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:11.010
So let's start out with an old two-inch brush today.

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:14.450
I'm gonna go right into a small amount of the phthalo blue.

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:17.750
Just tap a tiny bit of it into the bristles.

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:20.090
Just pull a little paint out and tap it.

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:24.020
The tapping assures that we have an even distribution

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:26.160
of color all the way through the bristles.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:27.830
Okay, let's go right up here.

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:30.000
Now maybe on this one, we'll just start

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.910
start up at the top and make little criss-cross strokes.

00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:38.350
We'll say the one over on this side is our summer scene.

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:43.360
So we'll just put in a happy blue little sky, just like so,

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.580
just using little criss-cross strokes.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:47.960
Now the canvases were both coated with liquid white,

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:51.340
so the liquid white is continually mixing with the color,

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:53.610
and that allows us to actually blend color

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:55.930
right on the canvas rather than working ourself to death

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:57.660
on the palette or the canvas.

00:01:57.660 --> 00:01:59.510
Take a small amount of Alizarin Crimson,

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:03.370
And maybe, maybe right in here,

00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:05.030
we'll just add a little touch of that.

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:07.540
It'll make a nice little lavender hue.

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:11.130
Right in there, just to sparkle it up again.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:15.130
There, okay, now then.

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:16.480
Without cleaning the brush,

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.390
let's go right over to the canvas,

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:20.200
and let's say it's winter.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:21.540
The other one will have winter.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.100
I'm gonna take phthalo blue,

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:24.160
and I'll reach right up here

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:27.120
and get a touch of the midnight black.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:28.260
Because this is winter,

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:30.000
I wanna gray the sky a little bit.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:31.480
I want to make it a little chillier,

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:34.460
a little more mood to it, okay?

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:37.590
And here, we'll just, once again,

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.920
use the little criss-cross strokes.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:41.710
And depending on what you want,

00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:43.650
you can add more of the black,

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:47.690
you can gray it down, or you can leave it brighter.

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:49.510
It all depends on you.

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:51.450
However you want your world to be,

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:54.340
that's the way it oughta be.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:58.280
Okay, that's a nice little gray sky there.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.000
So tell you what, let's take some of that same,

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.820
Just the black and the blue, that's all we need.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:06.020
And let's go down here and let's have a little water

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:09.020
in these paintings, what the heck, what the heck.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:13.570
Pull from the outside, inward, outside, inward.

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:16.660
There, both sides.

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:19.470
That way it'll leave a little open area right in here.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:21.520
And when it's all done, it'll look like a little sheen

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:23.520
of light coming across there.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:24.520
It'll be very pretty.

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:27.050
Now very gently, very gently.

00:03:27.050 --> 00:03:29.010
Three hairs and some air.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:30.000
We just go across here.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.400
and blend that.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.400
The little light area still remains in there.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.860
Okay, I'm going back into my phthalo blue,

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:38.290
and I'm going to add a touch,

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:41.440
and let me say that again, a touch of phthalo green.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:43.360
It's very strong, very strong.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:46.020
We'll go back to our summer canvas,

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:48.190
and let's do the same thing.

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:50.190
I put the green in there once again

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:51.300
to make this one a little brighter.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.300
This is summer, it's happier.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.790
Oh, the birds are having a good time.

00:03:55.790 --> 00:04:00.000
So that's what we want to show you.

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:03.070
over here, but still, pull from the outside in.

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:08.480
There we go, and very lightly, just go across.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:11.230
Okay, now we can wash the old brush.

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:13.730
And if you've painted with me before,

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:16.550
you know this is the fun part of this whole technique.

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:18.790
We wash our brushes with odorless thinner,

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:23.210
shake 'em off, and just beat the devil out of 'em.

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:25.330
And that's where you take all your hostilities

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:28.110
and frustrations, and it's a lot of fun.

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:30.000
Okay, let's put some on.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.290
some clouds in here, what the heck.

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:34.910
Take titanium white, let's do the summer one first.

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:37.610
We'll take white, be right back, right back.

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:40.650
Get a little touch of the bright red.

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:43.390
Little touch, not much, okay?

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:45.820
Maybe there lives in our world a little cloud

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:47.540
right up here.

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:51.780
We're making small, little, tiny, circular strokes.

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:57.610
Little, tiny circles, little, tiny circles, there we go.

00:04:57.610 --> 00:05:00.000
Just sort of let the cloud float around and have fun.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.960
She's got a little friend lives over here.

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:06.930
See how easy that is?

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:11.040
Now then, on the other side, in our winter scene,

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.300
I'm gonna add a touch of gray to it,

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:16.560
a little bit of the midnight black, just to gray it down.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:20.110
'Cause once again, we don't want this as bright.

00:05:20.110 --> 00:05:22.330
Now, maybe this old cloud lives right here,

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:23.960
and it just sort of floats around.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:27.090
There.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:29.830
When you're doing this, just sort of think like a cloud.

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:35.890
They're free and they have a good time and just enjoy it.

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:38.490
Little tiny circles, and don't overwork it.

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:40.980
If you overwork it, it'll begin looking like

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:43.020
a big cotton ball that lives up here in the sky.

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:46.410
We don't want that, we want some life in this son of a gun.

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:50.250
All right, now with a good clean dry brush,

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:54.950
I'm gonna gently, gently blend the base of these clouds.

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:57.600
Just blend the base of it.

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:59.160
There we go.

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:00.000
Now fluff 'em.

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:03.240
Grab 'em and fluff 'em.

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:07.100
And then very lightly blend the entire sky.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:10.270
And that easy, you've got a fantastic little cloud.

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:11.330
And while we're going here,

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:14.130
let's do the little summer scene over here.

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:16.990
Same basic thing.

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:20.810
Fluff it, pull it, lift it.

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:25.050
There, very gently though.

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:27.160
There we go.

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:30.000
Now then, let's have some fun.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.350
in our world today, maybe this little mountain back here.

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:33.860
I like to paint mountains.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:35.500
I lived in Alaska for a dozen years,

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:38.170
and mountains are very, oh, they're very special to me.

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:41.860
I like them, so we'll take some black, Van Dyke Brown,

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:43.420
put a little alizarin crimson in it,

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:47.800
and a little bit of the Prussian blue, very strong blue.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:52.490
Pull the paint out very flat, go straight down with a knife,

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:54.590
cut across, and that gives us a little roll of paint

00:06:54.590 --> 00:06:57.420
right out of the edge of the knife.

00:06:57.420 --> 00:06:59.230
Now you have to make a major decision.

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:00.000
Where does your mountain live?

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:03.800
maybe in our world, lives right here.

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:06.850
And I want this mountain to be quite small.

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:09.900
Just a little tiny mountain that's far away.

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:13.580
So all we need is just a basic little shape.

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:17.090
Maybe this little bump lives right there.

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:19.240
The only thing we're concerned with

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:20.380
is the nice outside edge.

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:22.620
We could care less what's happening down here.

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:23.920
Don't worry about that.

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:26.610
We'll take care of that, don't worry about it.

00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:28.690
Now over here, we'll use the same color.

00:07:28.690 --> 00:07:30.000
And we'll try to make a mountain that looks

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.920
Looks about the same.

00:07:32.920 --> 00:07:39.260
We're trying to do the same scene in winter and summer.

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:44.340
We'll make 'em look similar here.

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:48.880
Okay, maybe right there.

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:51.120
Once again, we're only worried about the top of the mountain.

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:51.960
We could care less.

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:55.550
Down here, scrape off all the excess paint.

00:07:55.550 --> 00:07:57.700
Just scrape it off.

00:07:57.700 --> 00:08:00.000
Then with a large brush, we wanna grab this

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.490
and move it.

00:08:01.490 --> 00:08:03.130
Because the liquid whites on the canvas,

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:06.060
you can literally move the paint.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:07.830
If this was a dry canvas,

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:10.580
you'd be in agony city right now.

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:12.320
And just blend it down.

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:14.800
Same thing over here on this one.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:16.760
Grab it and pull it.

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:18.680
Just pull it.

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:21.240
Think about the angles in your mountain.

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:24.770
There we go.

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:27.180
And just let it blend right into nothing,

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:29.280
just like it's laying in the mist down here.

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:34.050
Now then, we'll go back to our knife.

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:35.490
And, tell you what, let's do.

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:39.670
We'll take some titanium white, dark sienna,

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:40.770
and we'll mix them together.

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:44.660
But leave it marbled like that, don't over mix.

00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:46.140
Cut off our little roll of paint.

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:48.280
It's right down the edge of the blade there.

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:49.220
Let's go up here.

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:53.240
Now this one over here, it has the summer scene on it.

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:57.460
Here, I want some nice browns on it

00:08:57.460 --> 00:09:00.000
and all kinds of things happening, and by not

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.620
Overmixing the paint, this happens automatically.

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:07.440
You get all kinds of beautiful colors and shades and tones.

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:09.460
You could work yourself to death trying to do this

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:11.880
by mixing each color.

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:14.390
This is a lazy man's way of painting.

00:09:14.390 --> 00:09:16.110
Let the canvas work.

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:18.340
Let the paint work.

00:09:18.340 --> 00:09:20.920
Maybe we'll put a little bit right out there.

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:22.650
There we go.

00:09:22.650 --> 00:09:24.990
Now then, we need a shadow color for that.

00:09:24.990 --> 00:09:28.810
I'll just take some, oh, we'll use some dark sienna.

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:30.000
A little bit of the Prussian blue

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.240
in it, that'll gray it down.

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:35.720
Once again, we cut off that little roll of paint,

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:40.310
small amount of paint, and we'll just put in a shadow.

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:43.890
So all there is to it, just in the opposite direction.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:49.160
Just, see there, and you can create just the illusion

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:52.340
of all kinds of things happening in your world.

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:56.740
There we go, maybe right in here.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:59.730
Just let that come down, just like so.

00:10:00.730 --> 00:10:03.120
anywhere you want 'em.

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:07.010
Over here, a little bit.

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:09.210
Okay, now then we'll take a clean, dry brush.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:10.270
Be sure it's dry.

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:12.730
If it's not dry, you're gonna be upset with me

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:15.980
'cause your color's gonna sort of just mix together.

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:18.070
We just tap the base of it here.

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:21.260
We wanna create the illusion of mist.

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:25.060
Soft, misty areas down here at the base of the mountain.

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:27.360
Then we lift it up,

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:29.080
and that'll sort of bring it all together.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:33.500
There we go.

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:37.060
Alright, and that easy, we have a summer-type mountain.

00:10:37.060 --> 00:10:40.040
Now let's go over here to the cold side.

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:42.580
We'll take titanium white,

00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:44.540
and there's a little bit of that gray color left in it,

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:46.010
not much.

00:10:46.010 --> 00:10:47.980
Once again, our little roll of paint.

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:50.210
Snow on this mountain.

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:58.120
As they say in Alaska, the hawk has came.

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:00.000
The old hawk.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:03.570
Snow on the mountain.

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:07.990
And we'll just let that come right on out like that.

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:12.040
A little bit on this peak like we had on the other one.

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:15.510
Gotta make those little noises or it doesn't work.

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:17.460
There we are, let's take a little bit of the,

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:19.540
we'll use a little phthalo blue,

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:24.420
a little touch of the black in it, a little white.

00:11:24.420 --> 00:11:26.720
We'll make a happy little shadow color, once again,

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:30.000
right on the edge of the knife.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:34.560
that zoom, but absolutely no pressure, no pressure.

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:39.290
It just floats across there.

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:41.590
As I've mentioned before in other shows,

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:44.550
when I was teaching my son Steve to paint,

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:46.630
I used to tell him to just pretend

00:11:46.630 --> 00:11:49.390
that he was a whisper floating across here.

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:52.090
It's that delicate of a touch.

00:11:52.090 --> 00:11:56.420
Just barely touch the canvas.

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:58.360
Okay, now then, we'll tap this.

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:04.030
just to create that old illusion of mist again.

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:09.360
Just touch it, like so.

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:12.470
Okay, now then, maybe there's some,

00:12:12.470 --> 00:12:14.430
maybe there's some little foothills that live back here.

00:12:14.430 --> 00:12:17.950
So let's take, we'll use some,

00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:20.110
oh, some black and a little brown.

00:12:20.110 --> 00:12:24.160
I'm gonna reach up here, get a little touch of the sap green.

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:27.070
Not too much green, a little bit of white,

00:12:27.070 --> 00:12:30.000
just to lighten it up, okay.

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:30.870
Let's go up here.

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:32.520
Maybe on this one here,

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:35.850
we'll just touch with a corner of the two-inch brush

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:39.440
and just make the indication of little distant foothills

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:44.020
that live far, far away.

00:12:44.020 --> 00:12:47.660
Just touching.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:50.780
Now then, if there's gonna be water down here,

00:12:50.780 --> 00:12:51.780
let's have a reflection.

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:53.600
So all we'll do is just tap some of that color

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:57.920
right down like so.

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:00.000
All right, that's coming along nice.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:04.710
Now take the big brush, pull straight down, straight down.

00:13:04.710 --> 00:13:09.270
Look at there, look at there, instant reflections.

00:13:09.270 --> 00:13:10.470
When I was a traditional painter,

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:12.670
reflections used to drive me crazy.

00:13:12.670 --> 00:13:13.850
And it's one of the easiest things

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:15.990
you can do in this technique.

00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:18.210
All right, let's put some over here on the winter side.

00:13:18.210 --> 00:13:20.190
We'll take some white, some white,

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:22.270
I'm gonna grab some black.

00:13:22.270 --> 00:13:25.060
There we are, a little bit of black.

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:27.850
Least little touch of blue.

00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:29.890
We want these to be gray.

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:33.720
Once again, this is winter, it's a little more drab.

00:13:33.720 --> 00:13:35.940
Okay, let's go right up here.

00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:40.620
Now, same basic shape, we'll just tap in.

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:43.140
There we are, all there is to it.

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:47.340
Just think in your mind where a little foothill lives

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:51.730
and put it in, put it in.

00:13:51.730 --> 00:13:54.150
This is your world on this piece of canvas

00:13:54.150 --> 00:13:56.910
and you can do anything that your heart desires here.

00:13:56.910 --> 00:13:59.410
You have absolute and total power.

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:02.770
This is the only place in the world I have any power.

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:05.170
But here, here I'm the dictator.

00:14:05.170 --> 00:14:07.800
Boy, I can do anything here, anything.

00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:09.250
And you can too.

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:13.680
Just think of a scene in your mind

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:16.520
and put it on canvas.

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:19.780
That easy we have a happy little reflection.

00:14:19.780 --> 00:14:21.310
I'm gonna dip the knife into a little bit

00:14:21.310 --> 00:14:23.530
of the liquid white.

00:14:23.530 --> 00:14:26.080
Just pull that through.

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:28.340
Be right back, get a little touch of crimson.

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:29.890
Shoot, we'll brighten this one up.

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:33.080
Pull it out and then cut across, just like that.

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:35.060
Let's go up here.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:38.560
Now then, let's put in just a happy little water line.

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:40.320
And we act just like we're trying to cut a hole

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:42.190
in the canvas.

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:44.020
That's all there is to it.

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:48.010
Just a little ripple here and there.

00:14:48.010 --> 00:14:52.940
Okay, on the other side I'm using just straight

00:14:52.940 --> 00:14:54.540
liquid white.

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:55.700
Don't want the pink over there.

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:57.360
I want this one to be a little colder.

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:05.220
See there, it's that easy though.

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:07.550
You can do it, you can do anything.

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:11.580
Anything that the mind can conceive, you can do.

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:14.320
At least up here.

00:15:14.320 --> 00:15:18.650
All right, now we have to make some big decision.

00:15:18.650 --> 00:15:22.210
What lives up in the foreground here?

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:24.340
I'll tell you what, let's just get crazy.

00:15:24.340 --> 00:15:28.590
We'll take some black, some blue,

00:15:28.590 --> 00:15:30.000
I'll grab some alizarin crimson,

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:33.150
a little Van Dyke brown.

00:15:33.150 --> 00:15:34.470
I'm not using any green in this.

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:37.790
Then I'll use the same color on the both sides.

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:42.940
Just the blues, both blues and black, brown, crimson.

00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:44.630
Okay, let's go right up here.

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:51.340
Maybe there lives in our world a nice tree, big tree.

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:55.830
And he lives here and he watches everything.

00:15:55.830 --> 00:15:58.260
Just push, bend the brush upward.

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:02.180
There we go.

00:16:02.180 --> 00:16:04.100
Maybe there's, shoot, maybe there's a little land

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:06.460
that comes right across here.

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:11.630
I don't know, just whatever you want.

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:16.930
Here you can create any illusion that pleases you.

00:16:16.930 --> 00:16:20.780
All we're doing is just filling that in.

00:16:20.780 --> 00:16:23.980
Now then, pull the brush in one direction

00:16:23.980 --> 00:16:25.450
when you're doing this, see?

00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:26.610
One direction.

00:16:26.610 --> 00:16:28.470
That causes a curve.

00:16:28.470 --> 00:16:30.000
You turn the brush over so that curves

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.130
to the top, now let's go up here.

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:34.460
Let's push in a tree over here on the winter scene.

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:37.420
Same basic tree, maybe we'll do one over here

00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:39.790
that's all covered with snow.

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:41.980
Ooh, cold over here on this side.

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:45.120
You have to wear a coat when you paint this one.

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:49.090
Just like so.

00:16:49.090 --> 00:16:54.130
Tell you what, just so you have some practice,

00:16:54.130 --> 00:16:57.720
let's do this, find a fan brush there.

00:16:57.720 --> 00:17:00.000
Let's do a happy little evergreen tree too.

00:17:00.030 --> 00:17:02.970
We'll use some blue and some black and brown and crimson,

00:17:02.970 --> 00:17:06.220
just those same colors, same old colors.

00:17:06.220 --> 00:17:07.860
Load the brush full of paint.

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:09.550
Let's go right up here.

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:13.600
Maybe in our world, there lives, does now,

00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:16.330
just a happy little evergreen tree.

00:17:16.330 --> 00:17:19.800
Just go back and forth, back and forth, see?

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:21.560
They live here in your fan brush.

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:23.920
Sometimes you have to sort of scare 'em out.

00:17:23.920 --> 00:17:29.230
There we go, there we go, see?

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:30.000
And leave some more.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:32.840
like this so the birds have a place to sit when they come.

00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:37.690
And he goes down here somewhere.

00:17:37.690 --> 00:17:38.850
We don't know where he goes.

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:44.270
Over here, let's put one about the same height

00:17:44.270 --> 00:17:49.020
and we'll just drop him in.

00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:52.960
These little paintings will give you a lot of practice,

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:55.520
show you how to do all kinds of different things,

00:17:55.520 --> 00:17:57.700
use all the equipments, all the colors.

00:17:57.700 --> 00:18:00.000
We only use about a dozen

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:03.040
and colors, 13 to be exact.

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:07.400
And with those 13 colors, you can do anything.

00:18:07.400 --> 00:18:11.010
It's unreal, unreal, what you can do.

00:18:11.010 --> 00:18:12.960
Maybe, see sometime you change your mind.

00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:16.600
Maybe there needs to be a little baby tree right here.

00:18:16.600 --> 00:18:18.970
Don't want that tree to get lonely.

00:18:18.970 --> 00:18:22.220
So we can just put him in.

00:18:22.220 --> 00:18:25.850
And when you do your painting, let's go over here.

00:18:25.850 --> 00:18:28.490
When you do your painting, you just sort of look at it

00:18:28.490 --> 00:18:30.000
and you decide how many trees

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:31.820
live in your world.

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:38.530
You can have two, ten, zero, any number in between.

00:18:38.530 --> 00:18:41.240
Any number in between.

00:18:41.240 --> 00:18:43.720
Now since this is a winter scene over here,

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:45.220
we need some snow on the ground.

00:18:45.220 --> 00:18:47.560
So let's just take titanium white on the big brush,

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:52.080
just pull some in there, just like so.

00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:54.590
Now then, decide where your snow lives.

00:18:54.590 --> 00:19:00.000
Maybe it lives right here under the trees, just like so.

00:19:02.460 --> 00:19:04.460
That's what's great about this old big brush.

00:19:04.460 --> 00:19:07.310
You can just do it quick.

00:19:07.310 --> 00:19:09.360
See, allow some of that dark color

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:11.790
to pick up and pull it.

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:15.910
Then it looks like shadows under these bushes and trees.

00:19:15.910 --> 00:19:21.130
Okay, now then let's start having some fun.

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:22.900
Maybe we'll highlight this.

00:19:22.900 --> 00:19:24.860
So, I'm gonna dip the brush into a touch

00:19:24.860 --> 00:19:27.730
of the liquid white on the one inch brush.

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:29.670
And let's start out, we'll go through

00:19:30.030 --> 00:19:32.930
cad yellow, let's do the summer one first.

00:19:32.930 --> 00:19:35.450
Just cad yellow, it'll be right back, don't go away.

00:19:35.450 --> 00:19:40.620
Right there, a little bit of the sap green added to it.

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:42.180
Pull the brush in one direction though,

00:19:42.180 --> 00:19:44.490
and look at the amount of paint that's in the bristles.

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:47.160
Tremendous amount of paint.

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:49.360
That's what you need, okay.

00:19:49.360 --> 00:19:50.900
Now if you have a lot of paint in here,

00:19:50.900 --> 00:19:52.420
and it's a thin paint, this is thinner

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:53.960
than the paint that's already on the canvas,

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:56.680
we use a very firm dry paint up here.

00:19:56.680 --> 00:20:00.000
Now this is thin, now all you need is a gentle

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.690
little touch, and you can put beautiful highlights

00:20:02.690 --> 00:20:07.000
out here on your tree, beautiful highlights.

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:08.870
But now think like a tree.

00:20:08.870 --> 00:20:11.990
Tree has limbs, it has little arms that live in here.

00:20:11.990 --> 00:20:15.530
Don't just, don't just stab these on at random.

00:20:15.530 --> 00:20:16.890
Think about shape.

00:20:16.890 --> 00:20:20.400
There's little branches and stuff that live inside of here,

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:25.220
and they're little individuals, they each have a personality.

00:20:25.220 --> 00:20:26.660
Okay, and we can add a little yellow ochre,

00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:30.000
a little Indian yellow here and there.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.800
maybe a little touch of the bright red just to sparkle it.

00:20:32.800 --> 00:20:40.720
Okay, a little touch of bright red.

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:43.470
Shoot, maybe there's a firecracker lives right out here.

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:46.650
Mm, boy, that's pretty, that's pretty.

00:20:46.650 --> 00:20:51.310
Son of a gun, see, but working layers.

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:54.070
Now then, come right up in here.

00:20:54.070 --> 00:20:56.920
Notice that we leave some of the dark areas.

00:20:56.920 --> 00:21:00.000
Those little dark areas in between are very important.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:03.810
That's what gives your little bushes and trees depth.

00:21:03.810 --> 00:21:12.020
Okay, then, let's take, we'll use a fan brush here.

00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:14.800
I'll just take a little yellow,

00:21:14.800 --> 00:21:18.940
some sap green mixed in it, pretty dark color.

00:21:18.940 --> 00:21:20.790
Load a lot of paint in the bristles.

00:21:20.790 --> 00:21:23.060
And our evergreen tree here.

00:21:23.060 --> 00:21:27.940
Just add some little highlights on him, don't overdo.

00:21:27.940 --> 00:21:30.000
This gets working so well that you can

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:31.540
you just want to cover up all the dark

00:21:31.540 --> 00:21:35.330
and you lose your beautiful little tree then.

00:21:35.330 --> 00:21:39.750
It'll go away and leave you.

00:21:39.750 --> 00:21:42.160
Okay, now we, here's an old dirty,

00:21:42.160 --> 00:21:45.150
that's just two inch brush that's dirty.

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:47.830
We'll just tap it right into various colors.

00:21:47.830 --> 00:21:50.400
Just tap, give it a little push.

00:21:50.400 --> 00:21:53.700
Now then, let's come right down here

00:21:53.700 --> 00:21:55.400
and we can begin putting in all kinds

00:21:55.400 --> 00:21:58.180
of little happy grassy areas.

00:21:58.180 --> 00:21:59.020
That easy.

00:22:00.350 --> 00:22:02.920
That easy.

00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:05.820
Think about the lay of the land here.

00:22:05.820 --> 00:22:08.870
Just layer after layer after layer.

00:22:08.870 --> 00:22:12.490
Okay, maybe.

00:22:12.490 --> 00:22:15.220
So you can create a whole 'nother plane.

00:22:15.220 --> 00:22:22.720
Kill all that dark once again.

00:22:22.720 --> 00:22:25.730
It gets feeling good and you just go crazy.

00:22:25.730 --> 00:22:29.120
You can kill all that dark.

00:22:30.510 --> 00:22:33.080
and then your painting gets very, very flat.

00:22:33.080 --> 00:22:34.820
It looks like you, almost like you cut it out

00:22:34.820 --> 00:22:37.070
of newspaper or something and glued it up here.

00:22:37.070 --> 00:22:40.050
Now we just take a knife, clean knife,

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:41.450
and here and there we'll just scrape in

00:22:41.450 --> 00:22:43.850
the indication of some little sticks and twigs

00:22:43.850 --> 00:22:48.040
and little happy things that live all back in here.

00:22:48.040 --> 00:22:50.070
That's all there is to it.

00:22:50.070 --> 00:22:52.770
Let's do the other one now.

00:22:52.770 --> 00:22:55.120
Now, I have several fan brushes going

00:22:55.120 --> 00:22:58.260
so I don't have to spend all my time washing them.

00:22:58.260 --> 00:23:00.000
We'll take, we'll take some white,

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:01.150
I'll be right back.

00:23:01.150 --> 00:23:03.780
Little touch of the phthalo blue.

00:23:03.780 --> 00:23:06.850
Nice warm blue, very pretty.

00:23:06.850 --> 00:23:08.160
There.

00:23:08.160 --> 00:23:10.380
Okay, let's go up here.

00:23:10.380 --> 00:23:15.810
Maybe there's a little snow hanging on this tree.

00:23:15.810 --> 00:23:20.360
See, that's where the birds sit, right out here.

00:23:20.360 --> 00:23:24.280
Even in the wintertime, they have to have a place to sit.

00:23:24.280 --> 00:23:25.900
Sometimes when you paint it,

00:23:25.900 --> 00:23:28.230
you can almost hear the little birds.

00:23:32.810 --> 00:23:35.850
See, just once again, though, make up little stories

00:23:35.850 --> 00:23:38.420
and think that this is your world.

00:23:38.420 --> 00:23:42.770
It becomes a special place to you.

00:23:42.770 --> 00:23:44.630
And of course, people may look at you

00:23:44.630 --> 00:23:46.930
like you're a little strange, but us painters,

00:23:46.930 --> 00:23:48.330
you know, we have an artist's license

00:23:48.330 --> 00:23:50.770
and it says you can do anything on this canvas

00:23:50.770 --> 00:23:52.380
that makes you happy.

00:23:52.380 --> 00:23:53.760
Utilize that.

00:23:53.760 --> 00:23:57.330
We'll take titanium white and liquid white,

00:23:57.330 --> 00:24:00.000
mixed together on the brush, pull it in one direction.

00:24:00.250 --> 00:24:03.590
a lot of paint, a lot of paint.

00:24:03.590 --> 00:24:06.530
The liquid white's in there only to make the paint thinner.

00:24:06.530 --> 00:24:07.740
Let's go right up here.

00:24:07.740 --> 00:24:10.360
Put the rounded corner to the top,

00:24:10.360 --> 00:24:12.960
and let's just put all kinds of beautiful

00:24:12.960 --> 00:24:16.380
little snow-covered limbs out here.

00:24:16.380 --> 00:24:19.500
Now if you wanted to, you could just take your liner brush

00:24:19.500 --> 00:24:20.900
and just make like a tree trunk.

00:24:20.900 --> 00:24:23.760
Maybe all the leaves fell off in your world.

00:24:23.760 --> 00:24:25.620
I sort of like to have these snow-covered things.

00:24:25.620 --> 00:24:30.000
To me, it's just beautiful.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:31.690
I lived in Alaska.

00:24:31.690 --> 00:24:33.770
Everything looked like this in the winter at times,

00:24:33.770 --> 00:24:37.660
and it was maybe one of the most beautiful times

00:24:37.660 --> 00:24:40.610
of the year in Alaska.

00:24:40.610 --> 00:24:42.520
Cold.

00:24:42.520 --> 00:24:43.510
Oh, it's pretty.

00:24:43.510 --> 00:24:44.960
It is so pretty.

00:24:44.960 --> 00:24:47.600
God was having a good day when he made Alaska.

00:24:47.600 --> 00:24:52.950
Things were going right.

00:24:52.950 --> 00:24:55.280
And maybe down in here lives a little bush.

00:24:55.280 --> 00:24:58.120
There he is.

00:24:58.120 --> 00:25:00.000
Just make up all kinds of little stories.

00:25:01.310 --> 00:25:02.910
Maybe over here.

00:25:02.910 --> 00:25:07.220
See, you can put a little bush right there.

00:25:07.220 --> 00:25:09.300
Just wherever you want 'em.

00:25:09.300 --> 00:25:12.130
Now then, once again, with our clean knife,

00:25:12.130 --> 00:25:14.600
and come right up here with the camera.

00:25:14.600 --> 00:25:15.960
See this dark area?

00:25:15.960 --> 00:25:18.510
That's where you want to put your stems.

00:25:18.510 --> 00:25:19.870
You don't want to put 'em up here.

00:25:19.870 --> 00:25:21.010
Put 'em down in the dark area

00:25:21.010 --> 00:25:23.580
because that's where you'd see 'em.

00:25:23.580 --> 00:25:26.030
And just scratch 'em, just scratch 'em in.

00:25:26.030 --> 00:25:28.360
All you're doing is allowing the canvas to show through.

00:25:33.070 --> 00:25:35.420
Once again, though, mainly in these dark areas.

00:25:35.420 --> 00:25:37.620
We can come over here, drop in a couple,

00:25:37.620 --> 00:25:41.670
just wherever you want 'em.

00:25:41.670 --> 00:25:46.310
Okay, I'm gonna find the old liner brush,

00:25:46.310 --> 00:25:51.440
go into some paint thinner, some dark sienna,

00:25:51.440 --> 00:25:55.600
and we want this paint to be thin like ink.

00:25:55.600 --> 00:25:58.250
Turn the bristles, turn it.

00:25:58.250 --> 00:26:00.000
A liner brush has very long bristles

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:01.830
on it, loads a lot of paint.

00:26:01.830 --> 00:26:04.150
There we go.

00:26:04.150 --> 00:26:08.030
Okay, maybe in our world, right up here lives a little stick.

00:26:08.030 --> 00:26:12.420
Just take touch, and it helps here if you're a little nervous.

00:26:12.420 --> 00:26:14.120
Makes a much more interesting little stick

00:26:14.120 --> 00:26:16.920
than one that's just straight.

00:26:16.920 --> 00:26:18.310
Or I think so.

00:26:18.310 --> 00:26:20.730
Just, you sort of make the decision.

00:26:20.730 --> 00:26:23.240
Maybe in your world, you want all straight sticks.

00:26:23.240 --> 00:26:25.710
I like to have them with a little character.

00:26:25.710 --> 00:26:28.190
Okay, we can take that same color.

00:26:28.190 --> 00:26:29.800
Let's go over in the winter side.

00:26:30.640 --> 00:26:33.720
and maybe the little stick lives right here.

00:26:33.720 --> 00:26:36.790
See, there he is, there he is.

00:26:36.790 --> 00:26:40.560
You knew he was there.

00:26:40.560 --> 00:26:45.610
Just touch it, give it a little pull.

00:26:45.610 --> 00:26:47.440
That's all there is to it.

00:26:47.440 --> 00:26:51.770
And you can put 'em wherever you want 'em.

00:26:51.770 --> 00:26:55.300
And that's how easy it is to make two scenes at once.

00:26:55.300 --> 00:26:56.720
I'm gonna take a little more of the paint thinner,

00:26:56.720 --> 00:26:59.760
go into some bright red, and let's sign these.

00:27:01.950 --> 00:27:03.720
and just then you paint once again,

00:27:03.720 --> 00:27:06.750
just like it was ink.

00:27:06.750 --> 00:27:07.650
And you can sign it.

00:27:07.650 --> 00:27:11.940
We'll go step right over to the winter one, sign it.

00:27:11.940 --> 00:27:13.040
And I think we're all finished.

00:27:13.040 --> 00:27:17.470
We have two paintings today for the price of one.

00:27:17.470 --> 00:27:19.340
There we are.

00:27:19.340 --> 00:27:20.420
And I hope you've enjoyed this,

00:27:20.420 --> 00:27:23.440
and it shows you how to do a winter and a summer scene

00:27:23.440 --> 00:27:26.090
off the same palette at the same time.

